  "body": "Full-audit backend/performance follow-up on stable d5f50bc.\n\n- Bot daily-activity polling now uses a read-only quota snapshot instead of taking the bot row FOR UPDATE;\n- real reserve/release/getQuota mutation semantics remain unchanged and continue to use the write lock;\n- read-only snapshot still applies the same conservative durable usage floor, but never repairs rows during UI polling;\n- durable floor resolves audited reservation rows in one bulk findAllById call instead of one lookup per audit;\n- regression test verifies dashboard snapshot does not touch JdbcTemplate locking and does not persist a repair.\n\nNo quota limits, offer decisions, scheduler behavior, or frontend API shape changes.",
